{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And Moshe brought the people out to meet Elohim from the camp.</b> This is the camp of Israel, who were sixty myriad. <b>To meet Elohim.</b> Its meaning is: to meet the camp of Elohim — these are the ministering angels who descended there. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted that sixty myriad ministering angels descended there, corresponding to the sixty myriad of Israel, and to them Jacob alluded (Genesis 32:3): ״שם המקום ההוא מחנים״ — and he called the name of that place Machanayim, for the two camps stood opposite one another. And concerning this Solomon said: כמחולת המחנים. And because Israel was subjugated under the bondage of four kingdoms, and each of them said to Israel, 'Return to our faith and believe in us,' therefore he mentioned שובי four times. And we today are under the bondage of the fourth kingdom, which says: ״שובי ונחזה בך״ — meaning, we shall make rulers of you and give you every kind of dominion — and it is from the language of ״ואתה תחזה מכל העם״. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: השולמית — the nation in which the peace of the worlds dwells — and she replies: ״מה תחזו בשולמית״ — what dominion and greatness and honor can you give to the Shulamite? Can you possibly imagine in thought the joy of the standing at Mount Sinai? This is ״כמחולת המחנים״ — the two camps that went out to meet one another. And he likened the delight of the apprehension that they apprehended at that standing to a מחול, in the manner of what our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: the Holy One, blessed be He, is destined to make a מחול for the righteous in the Garden of Eden. And therefore: I have no wish to return to your faith, for I remember that מחול — meaning, the standing at Mount Sinai. And our Rabbis of blessed memory further interpreted that at that holy standing there were twenty-two thousand ministering angels, as is said (Psalms 68:18): ״רכב אלהים רבותים אלפי שנאן״, and these were those near to the Shekhinah more than the rest of the angels, and they corresponded to the twenty-two thousand Levites who were adjacent to the Tent of Meeting where the Ark was. And happy is the people for whom it is so, for they saw four living creatures of the Chariot inscribed in the word שנאן, and they saw four camps of the Shekhinah inscribed in the word ארגמן, for from what Solomon mentioned in his wisdom (Song of Songs 3:10): ״מרכבו ארגמן״, it will be explained to one who understands the secret of the One who rides upon four camps of the Shekhinah of glory, ארגמן. And it is known that from there they yearned for the standards. And they said in the Midrash that on that day of the giving of the Torah, the sun stood still and the dead were revived, as is written (Song of Songs 5): ״נפשי יצאה בדברו״, and so they interpreted in Eileh HaDevarim Rabbah: five times the sun stood still for Moshe — the day of the exodus from Egypt, and the day of the Sea, and the day of Amalek, and the day of the giving of the Torah, and the day of the wadis of Arnon — thus far." "<b>And they stood at the bottom of the mountain.</b> Below the mountain and outside the boundary from which they had been warned to keep their distance." "<b>And know</b> that the Glory was at the top of the mountain, as is said: ״וירד ה' על הר סיני אל ראש ההר״, and it is written (Exodus 24:17): ״ומראה כבוד ה' כאש אוכלת בראש ההר״. And all Israel stood at the foot of the mountain, as is said: ״ויתיצבו בתחתית ההר״. And Moshe merited to ascend the mountain to come within the cloud, as is said (Exodus 24:18): ״ויבא משה בתוך הענן ויעל אל ההר״. And he further merited to be brought near to עב הענן — the thickness of the cloud — which is what is written: ״הנה אנכי בא אליך בעב הענן״. And עב הענן is ערפל (the thick mist) which Elohim placed there, and this is what is elucidated in the verse (Deuteronomy 4:11): ״וההר בוער באש עד לב השמים חשך ענן וערפל״ — חשך is the fire, and after that ענן, and after that ערפל, which is עב הענן. According to this there were four levels, one above the other and one within the other, and these are: תחתית ההר (the bottom of the mountain), ראש ההר (the top of the mountain), ענן (cloud), and עב הענן (the thickness of the cloud). And we find their parallel in the Holy Temple: the gate of the courtyard corresponding to תחתית ההר, and the courtyard itself corresponding to the mountain itself, and the Sanctuary within corresponding to the interior of the cloud, and the Holy of Holies, which is within the Sanctuary, corresponding to עב הענן, which is the ערפל which Elohim placed there."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:22.730063317Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}